#!/bin/sh
snapshot="$("$HOME/.local/bin/antonina-scheduler-snapshot" 2>/dev/null || printf '{}')"
exec timeout -k 15s 240s "$HOME/.local/bin/opencode-openclaw" run --auto --model opencode-go/longcat-2.5-preview-free --variant low --dir /workspace/antonina "ANTONINA-SCHEDULER-TURN. Optimize ONLY for efficiency and topology: launch another agent whenever it has positive expected marginal wall-clock speedup after dependencies, overlap, collision risk, and reconciliation cost. NEVER inspect, infer, request, discuss, or reason about runtime or host capacity. Runtime capacity is outside scheduling. There is no global worker-count cap.

Use CURRENT_SNAPSHOT immediately. Reconcile duplicate live cwd ownership first. Then reason over the complete open-issue header list for project breadth. Do not rerun broad agent-list, board-list, board-feed, filesystem, or workspace-discovery scans unless the snapshot is missing or clearly stale. NEVER use ls/find/globs over /workspace to discover a cwd. CLI GRAMMAR IS STRICT: never pass issue IDs positionally. Never call 'antonina board show ISSUE' positionally. For a chosen candidate, read its body/newest comments with antonina board show --id ISSUE --page 1 --json; obtain registered cwd/worktree choices with antonina board resource list --issue ISSUE --page 1 --json; record claims with antonina board comment --id ISSUE --body BODY --author openclaw@marceline-dev --json; create with antonina agent new --id AGENT_ID --cwd CWD --title TITLE --json; start with antonina agent run --id AGENT_ID --cwd CWD --prompt PROMPT --detach --json; treat those paths only as topology/ownership metadata. Re-check selected live ownership immediately before launch.

Do not reread the scheduler skill during a routine turn; this launcher carries the hot-path policy. Establish project breadth first because independent projects normally have low reconciliation cost, then issue breadth, then useful intra-issue depth. After breadth, maintain project-local useful concurrency such as at least five AssemblyP1 agents when five positive-speedup fronts exist. Do not implement project work yourself. If this snapshot shows a clear project-breadth gap, this turn MUST NOT finish without either launching at least one missing-project owner or recording a precise dependency/topology/collision blocker. Machine/runtime capacity is NEVER a valid blocker. Launch useful detached agents only onto unoccupied cwd/worktrees, record exact ownership, keep launching while another front has positive expected marginal speedup, and return promptly.

CURRENT_SNAPSHOT:
$snapshot"
